            <ArticleTitle>A new class of ghrelin O-acyltransferase inhibitors incorporating triazole-linked lipid mimetic groups.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2800-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2015.05.009</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(15)00459-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inhibitors of ghrelin O-acyltransferase (GOAT) have untapped potential as therapeutics targeting obesity and diabetes. We report the first examples of GOAT inhibitors incorporating a triazole linkage as a biostable isosteric replacement for the ester bond in ghrelin and amide bonds in previously reported GOAT inhibitors. These triazole-containing inhibitors exhibit sub-micromolar inhibition of the human isoform of GOAT (hGOAT), and provide a foundation for rapid future chemical diversification and optimization of hGOAT inhibitors.</AbstractText>
